(; expect 1 ;)
(; Negative control: x is annotated with T, but its position (the body of z => x, where
   K z is expected) gives it the type U0, since K z reduces to U0.  An instance need not respect
   the annotation: g (f (z => u0)), of type T, would rewrite to u0, of type U0.  Taking the
   annotation's conversion to the position's type as a typing hypothesis would admit the rule. ;)
U0 : Type.
T : Type.
D : Type.
u0 : U0.
def K : D -> Type.
[z] K z --> U0.
f : (z : D -> K z) -> T.
def g : T -> T.
[x : T] g (f (z => x)) --> x.
